/P 264 0 R
/E (NSS volunteers helped the students for filling up their acknowledgment forms for the camp. There were a large number of students were present during the camp for getting their blood tested. About 200 students from various branches and semesters provided their blood samples for testing. Time slots were arranged for students according to their department for the ease of collection of blood samples. The medical team administered to collect the blood samples from thestudents. Awareness was created among the students regarding thalassemia, its types and the effects of this blood disorder in our life. The importance of thalassemia testing was also elaborated. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [10]
